#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Single-file bootstrap for the Giovanni: Rocket Rise GBA hack.
Run in a GitHub Codespace (Ubuntu):   python3 bootstrap.py
  1. unpacks all project files into the current folder (overwrites older copies)
  2. installs the ARM toolchain with apt (needs sudo)
  3. runs sandbox_kit/build_and_test.sh  -> build.log, install.log, debug_report.txt, giovanni_<stamp>.gba, shots/
Use --extract-only to skip steps 2 and 3. Do not commit any .gba ROM.
Re-running on an existing decomp/ is fine: patches are idempotent and make is incremental.
Play the NEW giovanni_<stamp>.gba each time on a FRESH save: old saves from older builds can crash newer ones.
NEW GAME STARTS INSIDE MOM'S HOUSE (opening scene lives in the home map script).
debug_report.txt (plain text, written automatically) holds the compiled scripts for the HQ-fight freeze: upload it.
TEST OPTION: a Level 10 Mewtwo is added as your first Pokemon by default for playtesting
  (Level 10 is the obedience cap with no badges). Turn it off with:  GIO_TEST_MEWTWO=0 python3 bootstrap.py
Crash-hunting mode (alley with no NPCs and no rain):  GIO_SAFE=1 python3 bootstrap.py
Sharing for review: python3 dump_reference.py decomp  -> reference/ (readable text incl. compiled scripts), then commit + push.
"""
